+#### signal
+
+Type: `AbortSignal`
+
+Cancel queued tasks when the signal is aborted.
+
+Queued tasks are rejected with the signal's [`reason`](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/API/AbortSignal/reason) and any task added afterwards is rejected immediately.
+
+Note: This does not cancel tasks that are already running.
+
+```js
+import pLimit from 'p-limit';
+
+const controller = new AbortController();
+const limit = pLimit({concurrency: 2, signal: controller.signal});
+
+const promises = urls.map(url => limit(() => fetch(url)));
+
+controller.abort();
+
+// Tasks that never started are rejected with `controller.signal.reason`
+const results = await Promise.allSettled(promises);
+```
+
 ### limit(fn, ...args)

 Returns the promise returned by calling `fn(...args)`.
